.TH TIDETOP 1 "2026-11-18" "tidetop 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tidetop \- a tidepic scene in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tidetop
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tidetop init
.I folder
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tidetop
shows a number as a scene instead of a chart. It is meant to sit in a corner of a
terminal and be read at a glance: whether things are roomy or tight right now,
rather than the exact value.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-data ,
it reads this computer's CPU (and memory with
.BR \-M ).
With
.BR \-\-data ,
it reads a tidepic feed from a file or an https URL.
Values are checked and computed by the tidepic runtime before a scene sees them.
.PP
The scenes
.B grove
and
.B stars
read
.I headroom
(100 minus CPU use), so they draw less when the computer is busy.
When headroom falls below 10% they draw flickering lines like a broken monitor.
.SH SCENES
.TP
.B campfire
One value (CPU use). The busier, the larger the fire.
.TP
.B grove
Headroom. The default scene. Roomy: leaves, green ground, a full pond, a waterfall, clouds.
Tight: bare branches and dry ground, still. Skins:
.B night
(default) and
.BR day .
.TP
.B stars
Headroom. Roomy: a clear sky, the Milky Way, twinkling stars, meteors, an aurora near the top.
Tight: clouds cover a dark sky. Skins:
.B milkyway
(default) and
.BR galaxy .
.TP
.B tide
Two values: memory (water level) and CPU (roughness).
.TP
.B windows
One lit window per CPU core.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-scene " name"
Scene to show:
.BR grove ,
.BR stars ,
.BR campfire ,
.BR tide ,
.BR windows .
.TP
.BI \-\-data " file|url"
Read a tidepic feed. A file is read again every second. An https URL is asked no
more often than every 10 seconds, or the feed's
.B meta.ttl
if longer. Plain http is not accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-art " folder"
Use a folder of text pictures as the scene. See
.BR "TEXT PICTURES" .
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use a pretend value that rises and falls every 40 seconds instead of real numbers.
Headroom scenes stay below the 10% line for about 4 seconds at the bottom.
Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-data .
.TP
.BI \-\-skin " name"
The scene's look. grove:
.BR night ,
.BR day .
stars:
.BR milkyway ,
.BR galaxy .
.TP
.B \-\-quality low|high
.B high
uses half blocks and Braille dots with 24-bit colour and needs UTF-8.
.B low
uses ASCII and up to eight colours. Picked from the terminal if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " n"
Frames per second, 1 to 60. Default 15 for high, 2 for low.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-mem
Start on memory instead of CPU. Only for scenes that read one value
(campfire, grove, stars, text pictures). Same as key
.BR m .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-top
When the headroom shown stays at or below a line for some seconds, close tidetop
and run
.BR top (1)
in its place. Not available on Windows.
It does not come back. When top ends, tidetop ends. Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-data .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-top\-below " \fIpercent\fR"
The line for
.BR \-t .
Default 20.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-top\-after " \fIseconds\fR"
How long
.B \-t
waits below the line. Default 5. 0 switches at once.
.TP
.BI \-\-grid " across" x down
Join several windows into one picture split into
.I across
by
.I down
pieces. See
.BR "JOINED WINDOWS" .
Only for grove and stars.
.TP
.BI \-\-pos " n"
The piece this window draws, counted from the top left: 1, 2, ... (2x2 is 1 2 / 3 4).
.TP
.B \-\-once
Print one frame and exit. Outside a terminal, give the size with
.B COLUMNS
and
.BR LINES .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH KEYS
Keys are not case-sensitive.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " n
Next scene: grove, stars, campfire, tide, windows. The value the scene reads is read again at once.
Not with
.B \-\-art
or in a joined window.
.TP
.B space
Read the value now. An https feed is not asked again within its floor (10 seconds or meta.ttl).
.TP
.B s
Change the read interval in turn: 0.5, 1, 2, 5 seconds; for https feeds 10, 30, 60 seconds.
.TP
.BR p " / " m
Read CPU / memory. Only for scenes that read one value and only for this computer.
.TP
.BR 1 ", " c
Split the screen into one piece per CPU core. Press again to go back.
From memory, it switches to CPU first. Pieces smaller than 8 by 3 cells are not made.
.TP
.B z
Change the skin.
.TP
.B i
Show or hide a status line at the bottom right, for example
.BR "[CPU 12% | grove]" .
Hidden by default.
.TP
.B t
Close tidetop and run top now. Not available on Windows.
.TP
.BR h ", " ?
Show or hide the key help.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.SH JOINED WINDOWS
Put terminal windows of several computers side by side. Each draws one piece of a
large picture with its own computer's value, so only a busy computer's piece dries
out or shows caution lines. The windows do not talk to each other.
.PP
The large picture is this window's size times the number of pieces, so the piece
always fills the window. Windows should share the same aspect ratio for the edges
to meet. Motion follows the wall clock, so pieces line up when the clocks agree.
.PP
.nf
tidetop \-\-scene grove \-\-grid 2x2 \-\-pos 1   # top left
tidetop \-\-scene grove \-\-grid 2x2 \-\-pos 3   # bottom left
.fi
.SH TEXT PICTURES
.B tidetop init
.I folder
writes eleven sample pictures (a campfire,
.B 0.txt
to
.BR 100.txt )
and a README.txt. It does not write into a folder that is not empty.
.PP
In a picture folder, each
.IB number .txt
is a picture. A picture shows when the value is at least its number.
Below the smallest number, the smallest picture shows. Files without a number
in the name are skipped.
.PP
Numbers use the value's own units. Without
.BR \-\-data ,
the value is CPU use in percent (0 is idle). For a 0\(en10 feed use
.B 0.txt
to
.BR 10.txt ;
for on and off,
.B 0.txt
and
.BR 1.txt .
.PP
A line holding only
.B \-\-\-
splits a file into frames, shown two per second.
Pictures are centred and cut where they do not fit. Wide characters such as
Hangul take two cells; emoji become
.BR ? .
Terminal control codes are removed. Up to 200 files of 64KB and 32 frames each
are read once at start.
.SH LOAD
tidetop writes only the cells that changed, looks four times a second while the
screen is still, and draws 15 frames a second by default. On an M-series Mac at
120\(mu40 cells it used about 0.3\(en3% of one core and 13\(en16MB of memory
(started directly; through npm, Node stays running beside it).
Lower
.B \-\-fps
or use
.B \-\-quality low
to use less.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Draw without colour.
.TP
.BR LANG ", " LC_ALL
Messages are in Korean when the locale starts with
.BR ko .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tidetop
tidetop \-\-scene stars
tidetop \-\-scene grove \-\-skin day \-t \-m 25 \-d 3
tidetop \-\-data https://tidepark.com/feed/sample/campfire
tidetop init ~/my\-art && tidetop \-\-art ~/my\-art
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1)
